"""Keep reviewed data boundaries and version migration guidance through regeneration."""
from product_api_review import ROOT

SECTIONS = {'api-reference/monitoring-design.mdx': '## Compare the same evidence scope\n\nMonitoring baseline metrics and `analyses.changes` use the same comparability checks: borrower, account and entity scope, connected sources, currency, accounting basis, exclusions, calculation and definition versions, and equal-length chronological periods. Related-party identity and source scope is finalized before comparison. Related-party finances do not become primary-business financial inputs. Incompatible observations return a reason and no numeric delta; unchanged, comparable observations can correctly return zero.\n\n`MonitoringRun.started_at` records evaluation start and `completed_at` records completion after result publication. Their difference measures evaluation processing, not queue wait, provider collection time or a latency guarantee.\n', 'api-reference/large-results.mdx': '## Consent on derived alerts\n\nCurrent source authorization applies to both the current and previous packages referenced by a monitoring alert. If either package has a revoked or expired source, the alert read returns `403 forbidden`; an alert list containing such an alert also returns `403`. Console retains restricted audit metadata and hides financial values, messages and evidence links. A historical baseline does not preserve access after consent withdrawal.\n', 'api-reference/underwriting-dimensions.mdx': '## Chargeback stage and method version\n\n`chargeback_amount_share` method `amlok-chargeback_amount_share-2` divides gross disputed **chargeback-stage** exposure by captured sales in the matched assessment-period cohort. `NormalizedDisputeRead.stage` distinguishes `inquiry`, `chargeback` and `unknown`. Disputes must have opened before period end. Their workflow status, including `needs_response`, `under_review`, `won`, `lost` or `closed`, does not change cohort membership. Inquiries are excluded; disputed exposure is not realized loss. Missing stage remains unsupported, never inferred from a resolution label.\n\nPreviously published packages retain their original method and values. Comparisons across method versions are unavailable. Publish a new immutable policy version using the method returned by configuration if a policy pins the older chargeback method; it is not silently evaluated using the new method.\n', 'sandbox/businesses-and-scenarios.mdx': '## Refresh existing collected observations\n\nNew samples identify chargebacks and pre-chargeback inquiries explicitly with `stage`. Existing evidence and completed results remain immutable. To collect the updated example for an existing sample business, request an explicit source sync and create a new assessment; alternatively reset the Sandbox to samples if you intend to replace its test records. A deployment does not rewrite earlier evidence or pretend that an unavailable input was observed.\n'}

def write_guides():
    for name, section in SECTIONS.items():
        page=ROOT/name
        text=page.read_text()
        heading=section.split('\n',1)[0]
        text=text.split(heading,1)[0].rstrip()
        page.write_text(text+'\n\n'+section.rstrip()+'\n')
